{
  "case_id": "2022-22-506",
  "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Solicitor General (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "COVID-19 is the most devastating\npandemic in our nation's history and it has\ncaused enormous disruption and economic\ndistress. Over the past three years, millions\nof Americans have struggled to pay rent,\nutilities, food, and many have been unable to\npay their debts.\nTo head off immediate harm for\nstudent-loan borrowers, two Secretaries across\ntwo administrations invoked the HEROES Act to\nsuspend interest and payment obligations for all\nAmericans with federally held loans. But, if\nthat forbearance ends without further relief,\nit's undisputed that defaults and delinquencies\nwill surge above pre-pandemic levels."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nebraska Solicitor General (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The states ask this Court to deny that\nvital relief to millions of Americans, but they\nlack standing to seek that result. They\nprincipally assert harm to a separate legal\nperson, MOHELA, that could sue in its own name\nbut has chosen not to do so, and the states'\nasserted harms to their tax revenues are\nself-inflicted and indirect. The states' bare\ndisagreement with this policy is not the sort of\nconcrete injury that Article III demands.\nOn the merits, the states say the Act\ndoesn't authorize the Secretary to ever forgive\nloan principal. But the Secretary's\ninterpretation of this text is not just a\nplausible reading; it's the best reading."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General, is this a\nwaiver, or is it a modification?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: General, the\namount at issue, the Chief mentioned the quarter\ntrillion dollars or the half a trillion dollars.\nHow do you deal with that? Because that seems\nto favor the argument that this is a major\nquestion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: And General, let's say\nthat nobody in Congress was aware that there is\nsuch a thing in our case law called the major\nquestions doctrine. So put that out of their\nminds.\nAnd you simply polled every member of\nCongress and asked that person whether, in\nthe ordinary sense of the term, they would regard\nwhat the government had -- proposes to do with\nstudent loans as a major question or something\nother than a major question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: No, but the question would be whether MOHELA is part of the State of Missouri for present purposes. And where we're considering injury in fact, why should the test turn solely or why should the lack of corporate status be a necessary element? Why shouldn't the test be something more like whether the relationship between this entity and the State of Missouri is such that an injury to MOHELA will necessarily or presumptively be an injury to the state?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: I don't think that those factors should count as important in the analysis, and to the extent the Court is inclined to broaden out the analysis beyond the principles I've articulated about corporate separateness, I think the most critical fact would be whether there's financial entanglement and whether Missouri has itself decided to blur those lines for purposes of making it responsible for MOHELA's own liabilities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: General, there was a Missouri case in 1979, Menorah Medical Center, with an agency much like MOHELA, and, there, the -- the Missouri Supreme Court said that that entity was not the state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: I think it's clear under state law, Justice Barrett, that Missouri doesn't have that kind of ownership interest in the assets of MOHELA. And I would point in particular to Missouri Revised Statute 173.410. This is the provision that makes clear that Missouri cannot take the assets of MOHELA and appropriate them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: And the argument is that you are, in effect, doing that without appropriations from Congress?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: In Pennsylvania, it was a tax credit that was going to be removed, so it's almost identical to this, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so we just think you don't need to go down the road of thinking about some of the broader arguments about tax injury in this case because it's so clear that this Court has already rejected the very injury the states are asserting under the Pennsylvania case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: General, my first question is clarifying because I think I may have misunderstood. You said at the start of your argument that the Secretary both waived and modified."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: So we don't know really what the ultimate loss would be to MOHELA, even if we believed that MOHELA is part of the state?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Could the Secretary say, well, there was this terrible earthquake and lots of people's houses were destroyed, and\nHeritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 118,
        "start": 118
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You don't think that fits within \"waiver\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 119,
        "start": 119
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Two questions, one on merits, one on standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 127,
        "start": 127
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what concerns me is that to the extent you're talking about separation of powers and major questions, the judiciary is part of the same constitutional separation of powers dynamic that compels us to think about questions like the major questions doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 127,
        "start": 127
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, there's never been a past use of the HEROES Act that would eliminate the amount that someone owes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so do -- do you dispute that the ordinary standing rule would be that a plaintiff cannot establish standing by asserting the interests of an independent actor or by saying that an independent actor not before the Court will respond to the defendant's actions in a certain way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't believe so. I think what we're asking for is the same treatment that the federal government got in Cherry Cotton Mills and Erickson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. So we'll go back and look at that case, and if we find that the federal government had some sort of a separate interest that it was asserting, do you lose? I mean, is that your only case that is going to make it be the case that we can find standing for you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 132,
        "start": 132
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Barrett, you asked about the provision of state law 173.420. This is a provision that refers generally to Missouri reserving rights over the assets of MOHELA. I think, if you look at that in context, it clearly functions as a savings clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 133,
        "start": 133
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MOHELA, which my friend has emphasized several times. That's actually one of the relevant questions under the arm-of-the-state doctrine, whether you could direct the authority in any way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-74ef07f01dda-0006-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 135,
        "start": 135
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no precedent in this Court's Article III doctrine to support that kind of broad expansion of Article III standing here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-22-506",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "74ef07f01ddaf411bc29ef47e67a8d4a6e8c0337d9107f95f56110414020743c",
